; Solarus for MiSTer — per-quest controller mapping.
;
; Sections are now GENERATED by scripts/quest_interrogate.py from each quest's own
; action names (see docs/quest-compatibility.md) -- run the interrogator against a
; quest's data and it emits a ready-to-paste [<quest-id>] section, no hand-authoring
; needed. Two sections below are the exception, kept HAND-HELD on purpose and must
; not be regenerated over:
;   * [zelda-roth-se-v1.2.1] -- ROTH's spare-slot layout (save on `select`, not the
;     generator's default slot order) was a considered human choice from reading the
;     quest's source, kept as shipped rather than reflowed to match the generator's
;     spare-slot rule.
;   * [patched-tunics-b007e656] -- the generator reproduces this section exactly (it
;     is the golden fixture the generator is tested against), so there is nothing to
;     regenerate; it stays hand-labeled as the source of truth.
;
; Quests listen for different keys, so one fixed table cannot serve them all:
;   * Mystery of Solarus DX uses stock Solarus GameCommands, whose default keyboard
;     bindings are exactly [default] below. It needs no section.
;   * Zelda ROTH SE also uses stock GameCommands for movement/attack/action/items/pause,
;     so [default] covers those. But scripts/game_manager.lua ALSO sets six quest-private
;     keyboard commands that live OUTSIDE GameCommands (save/quit, run, map, monster
;     list, look, commands screen) — [default] cannot reach those, so it has its own
;     section below mapping the three that matter most onto the three spare inputs.
;   * Patched Tunics runs its own input layer (lib/bindings.lua, mixed into the game
;     itself at zentropy.lua:730) that listens for a completely different set of keys.
;
; Syntax:
;   <input> = key <sdl key name> | none
;
;   inputs : right left down up a b x y l r select start
;   layers : built-in defaults, then [default], then [<quest-id>] (later wins, so a
;            quest section need only state its differences)
;   quest-id = the .sol filename without extension, e.g. patched-tunics-b007e656
;   comments start with ';'
;
; Edit this file on the SD card and relaunch the quest — no rebuild needed.

[default]
; Stock Solarus keyboard bindings (Savegame.cpp set_default_keyboard_controls).
right  = key right
left   = key left
down   = key down
up     = key up
b      = key c           ; attack
a      = key space       ; action
y      = key x           ; item_1
x      = key v           ; item_2
start  = key d           ; pause
l      = none
r      = none
select = none

[zelda-roth-se-v1.2.1]
; ROTH uses stock GameCommands for right/left/down/up/a/b/x/y/start (already covered
; by [default] above), but scripts/game_manager.lua:27-32 ALSO sets six quest-private
; keyboard commands read directly via sol.input.is_key_pressed()/key-event compare,
; outside GameCommands entirely — [default] cannot reach them. Only three pad inputs
; are spare (l, r, select; every other input is already claimed by GameCommands), so
; only three of the six get a mapping:
select = key escape        ; keyboard_save  — game:save(), ROTH's ONLY save/quit path
l      = key left shift    ; keyboard_run
r      = key p             ; keyboard_map
; Left unmapped for lack of spare inputs: keyboard_monsters = "m", keyboard_look =
; "left control", keyboard_commands = "f1". They stay reachable only by editing this
; file (e.g. swapping one of the three above) — not from any pad button out of the box.

[patched-tunics-b007e656]
; PT's own keys, from lib/bindings.lua. All seven of its actions are reachable here;
; the old hardcoded table reached only movement and action.
right  = key right
left   = key left
down   = key down
up     = key up
b      = key s           ; attack
a      = key space       ; action
l      = key tab         ; map
r      = key w           ; inventory
y      = key a           ; item_1
x      = key d           ; item_2
start  = key escape      ; escape / save menu
select = none

; Mystery of Solarus DX has no section on purpose: it uses stock GameCommands, and
; [default] above is stock Solarus's own keyboard binding set. Zelda ROTH SE also uses
; stock GameCommands for its standard commands (so it inherits the same [default] rows),
; but see [zelda-roth-se-v1.2.1] above for the quest-private keyboard commands that
; GameCommands doesn't cover.

; Zelda: Oni Link Begins SE -- GENERATED by scripts/quest_interrogate.py from the
; quest's own action names (scripts/quests.tsv pins it by commit SHA, no tagged
; release exists yet). ONLY 3 of its 5 quest-private actions fit the 3 spare pad
; inputs; `monsters` and `commands` are left unmapped -- see the header comment
; below (reproduced verbatim from the generator's output).
;
; INERT SECTION -- DO NOT DEPLOY AS-IS. The header below, [zelda_olb_se], is the
; interrogator's directory-derived quest id, NOT a `.sol` filename -- section
; lookup matches the deployed .sol name without its extension (see the Syntax note
; above), and no .sol has been packaged for this quest yet. When Oni Link Begins SE
; is packaged, RENAME this header to that .sol's basename (no extension), the same
; way [zelda-roth-se-v1.2.1] and [patched-tunics-b007e656] are named above. Do not
; invent a version string for the header in the meantime -- the quest has no
; release tag, so there is nothing correct to put there. Until renamed, this
; section matches no quest id and has no effect.
[zelda_olb_se]
; Generated by scripts/quest_interrogate.py from this quest's own
; action names. Edit freely -- this file is read from the SD card.
; Left unmapped for lack of spare pad inputs: monsters, commands.
; Reach them by swapping one of the rows below.
l      = key escape
r      = key left shift
select = key p
